gpui.e.order.how = With Ordering on, a project whose design is ready shows Buy it in the thread's header. Buy it opens a buy thread. Its agent checks that every board and part is ready, asks you anything missing (quantities, finishes, where to ship), exports the manufacturing files into the project's mfg/ folder and sends them to Backplane's order server, which measures them and prices the exact order: manufacturing (boards, assembly, components and parts, with Backplane's fee included), shipping, and duties and taxes. The quote shows in the thread, and nothing is charged until you press Buy now and pay on Stripe's checkout page. A quote holds for 3 days. Prices are estimates: if the real cost turns out higher, you are asked before anything more is charged and can have a full refund instead; if it is lower, the difference is refunded. Once paid, the thread shows the order's progress (placed, shipped, tracking). With Ordering off, nothing about your projects leaves this machine for ordering. Price estimates add a rough "from $X" to Buy it, worked out from each part's size and options without sending any files.
gpui.e.fallback.note = Applies to all threads and bots, including delegates, routines and mail runs. Your chosen model runs first. At a confirmed usage limit, try entries after it; if the whole chain is unavailable, work pauses and asks for attention.
