gpui.f.claude.title = Sign in to Claude
gpui.f.claude.body = Backplane runs Claude Code, Anthropic's command-line agent, on this computer. Install it, then add an account below. Name it, for example Work or Personal, and press Connect. Open the link, sign in and paste the code Claude shows. Add as many accounts as you have. When one reaches its usage limit, Backplane moves the thread to another. Each thread keeps its own account, and the chip beside the model picker changes it. Use for new threads picks where new threads start. If a sign-in fails or the code expires, press Connect again. Backplane never copies your keys and never runs a paid request to check them.
gpui.f.codex.title = Sign in to Codex
gpui.f.codex.body = Codex is OpenAI's command-line agent. Install it, add an account below and press Connect. Backplane shows a link and a code to enter there, and the step turns done when Codex reports the sign-in. You need only one agent, so skip this step if you use Claude.
gpui.f.others.title = Other agents
gpui.f.others.body = Backplane also runs these agents. Each one signs in with its own command, in a terminal on this computer, and Backplane cannot check that sign-in. An agent that is not signed in says so in its first reply. Skip this step if you use Claude or Codex. Antigravity is listed in the model picker, but this build cannot install it yet.
