gpui.f.kicad.body = Agents use KiCad to read, change and check boards and schematics. Backplane draws boards itself, but it needs kicad-cli to plot and export them. Backplane KiCad is our build of KiCad with an editing API, so agents can edit a board in a running KiCad. Setup downloads it for you when no KiCad is found: it checks the download against its checksum and installs it in Backplane's own folder, with no administrator password. Stock KiCad 9 or later works for viewing and export.
gpui.f.kicad.ok.v = Status ok. Backplane KiCad {version} runs from {cli}. Agents can edit a board in a running KiCad.
gpui.f.kicad.ok = Status ok. Backplane KiCad runs from {cli}. Agents can edit a board in a running KiCad.
