gpui.f.local.code = This code names only this computer (127.0.0.1): another computer cannot reach it. Start the hub with Tailscale on, or set BACKPLANE_URL to an address the other machine can reach, then make a new code.
gpui.f.only.this = Only this computer
gpui.f.machine.title = Another machine
gpui.f.machine.body = Each computer you use runs its own hub. Linked hubs show each other's projects and threads in one sidebar, and work stays on the computer that owns it. Hubs never link by themselves, even on one Tailscale account. To link two: make a code here, enter it with this address on the other computer, then approve its request here. You can also run backplane pair --machine over ssh. Both computers need a network route to each other, usually Tailscale. A code works once, for ten minutes. To look at another hub without linking, use the hub list at the top of the sidebar or Settings, Hubs.
