gpui.f.remote.title = Restarts and updates
gpui.f.cont.on = On. Turns that a restart cuts short go on by themselves.
gpui.f.cont.off = Off. A restart stops running turns, and you start them again.
gpui.f.remote.body.package = The hub keeps running when you close the window, so agents finish their work. This hub is updated by the installer or package it came from. To update, run the install command again. Settings, Network and updates shows the version and the update channel. Settings, Threads sets what happens to running turns when the hub restarts.
gpui.f.remote.body.channel = The hub keeps running when you close the window, so agents finish their work. This hub checks for a new build every hour on the {channel} channel and installs it once no turn is running. If the new build fails its health check, the hub goes back to the one it had. Paired phones show the same line in their Settings. Settings, Network and updates shows the version and the update channel. Settings, Threads sets what happens to running turns when the hub restarts.
gpui.f.cont.restart = Continue after a restart
gpui.f.open.page = Open the page
gpui.f.open.page.note = Closes setup and opens Settings, Network and updates. Finish setup in the sidebar brings you back.
gpui.f.network.updates = Network and updates
gpui.f.project.title = Your first project
gpui.f.project.body = A project is a folder, usually with a KiCad project in it. Give a folder that exists to add it, or a new path to make it. In a git repository, each thread works in its own worktree, so threads do not touch each other's files.
gpui.f.add.another = Add another project.
gpui.f.path.folder = The path to a folder on this machine.
gpui.f.add.project = Add a project
gpui.f.create.project = Create the project
gpui.f.full.path = Give the full path, starting at the top of the disk.
gpui.f.thread.title = Your first thread
gpui.f.thread.body = A thread is one conversation with an agent, working in a project. Type what you want in the box at the bottom and press Enter. Pick the agent, model and effort with the picker beside the box. Agents ask before they run tools, unless you choose a looser mode in the same place.
gpui.f.new.thread.in = New thread in {project}
gpui.f.new.thread.note = You can start it empty and write in it after setup, or give it a first message.
gpui.f.start.thread = Start the thread
gpui.f.first.message = First message
gpui.f.project.first = Add a project first.
gpui.f.go.project = Go to the project step
gpui.f.n.so.far = {n, number} so far.
gpui.f.tour.viewers = Boards and schematics
gpui.f.tour.viewers.body = The rail beside a thread opens its project in a viewer. Backplane draws boards and schematics itself, so they open without KiCad running, and the view updates when an agent changes a file. Press a letter while the keyboard is outside the message box. The history bar under a view steps through each saved version.
gpui.f.key.side = Schematic and board side by side
gpui.f.key.diff = Diff of the thread's changes
gpui.f.tour.threed = 3D view
gpui.f.tour.threed.body = Press 3 for the board in 3D, with its parts. Drag to turn it in any direction and use the wheel to zoom at the pointer. A right drag, a middle drag or Shift with a drag moves it. The view redraws only while you move it, so an open 3D view uses no processor time at rest.
gpui.f.key.threed = 3D model
gpui.f.tour.mech = Mechanical parts
gpui.f.tour.mech.body = Press M for the Mech view. It lists every STEP file in the project's mech folder, such as an enclosure, a bracket or the board in a fit check, and draws the one you pick in 3D with the same controls. Agents write each part as a FreeCAD script beside its STEP, so FreeCAD has to be installed for them to change one.
gpui.f.tour.browser.body = Agents have a web browser on the hub's machine for datasheets, part pages and web tools. Press W to watch it. A bot's browser is also its Browser tab. This build shows the page the agent has open, and you cannot click in it yet.
gpui.f.tour.thread = Working in a thread
gpui.f.tour.thread.body = Settle takes a thread out of the active list and Snooze hides it until later. Fork starts a new thread from this one. Runs of tool calls fold into one row, and delegated work shows under Subagents. {m}+Shift+S settles and Ctrl+. stops a running turn.
gpui.f.tour.bots.body = A bot is an agent that stays between chats, with a name, a cat and a memory. Bots work across all your projects. Mention one in any message: @scout look at the BOM. Each bot has tabs for its chat, its space, its browser, its tasks, its memory, its routines and its webhooks.
gpui.f.make.bot = Make a bot
gpui.f.opens.form = Opens the form in the sidebar.
gpui.f.new.bot = New bot
gpui.f.tour.space = A bot's space
gpui.f.tour.space.body = Each bot has a Space tab, a page the bot writes for you with its space_set tool. It can hold a status, a table, buttons and fields to fill in, for example a parts list with an Order button. Ask the bot to build one: make me a space that tracks the open BOM questions. A new bot has an empty space.
gpui.f.tour.rooms.body = A room is a shared chat for you and your bots. Pick who joins, then post. Each bot reads the room and answers there, so two bots can review each other's work while you watch. Rooms work across linked machines too.
gpui.f.make.room = Make a room
gpui.f.new.room = New room
gpui.f.tour.routines.body = A routine runs a bot on a schedule. Open a bot, then its Routines tab, and write what it should do and when. Backplane reads times like tomorrow 9am, monday 09:00, in 20m or 2026-10-14 09:00. Routines follow your time zone, which Settings, Time zone shows. Reminders use the same list.
gpui.f.tour.palette = Palette and shortcuts
gpui.f.tour.palette.body = {m}+K opens the palette. Type part of a thread's name or a command, then press Enter. Settings, This device lists every shortcut and lets you change them.
gpui.f.key.agent = Agent, model and effort
gpui.f.key.prevnext = Previous and next thread
gpui.f.key.prevnext.keys = {m}+Shift+[ and {m}+Shift+]
gpui.f.key.uber = Uberbot chat
